IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgc2-common`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 6 Division 2, section 205 -- appointment and remuneration of auditors. LAYER 1 (the law, objectively).
--
-- Who may be an auditor is the keel's (s 10, sg-auditors.l4); this module takes "the person or firm appointed is an accounting
-- entity" as a plain fact. Every function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN unless it says otherwise: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the
-- text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say" (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sgc2)").
-- A function named "... is in default of the duty ..." answers JUST TRUE for a default and JUST FALSE for no default on the facts
-- (the provision's own question; fork line F-D1 in NOTES.md).

§ `Section 205: the acts and parties of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `s 205 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 205(1) appoint an accounting entity or accounting entities as the auditor or auditors of the company`
    `s 205(2) appoint an accounting entity or accounting entities as the auditor or auditors at the annual general meeting`
    `s 205(5)(a) send a copy of the notice of the resolution to remove the auditor to the auditor concerned and to the Registrar`
    `s 205(6) send a copy of the representations to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent`
    `s 205(8) give written notice of the removal of the auditor to the Registrar`
    `s 205(12) send a copy of the notice of nomination to the accounting entity nominated, to each auditor and to each person entitled to receive notice of general meetings`

§ `Section 205(1): the directors' duty to appoint the first auditor`

-- src:19073 | 205.—(1) The directors of a company must, within 3 months after
-- src:19074 | incorporation of the company, appoint an accounting entity or
-- src:19075 | accounting entities to be the auditor or auditors of the company, and
-- src:19076 | any auditor or auditors so appointed hold office, subject to this
-- src:19077 | section, until the conclusion of the first annual general meeting.
@ref s 205(1) (src:19073-19077)
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 205(1) the last day for the directors to appoint the first auditor` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the company was incorporated` 3 Months

-- src:19073 | 205.—(1) The directors of a company must, within 3 months after
-- src:19074 | incorporation of the company, appoint an accounting entity or
-- src:19075 | accounting entities to be the auditor or auditors of the company, and
-- src:19076 | any auditor or auditors so appointed hold office, subject to this
-- src:19077 | section, until the conclusion of the first annual general meeting.
@ref s 205(1) (src:19073-19077)
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the directors have appointed an accounting entity or accounting entities as the auditor or auditors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the directors made the appointment` IS A DATE
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(1) the directors are in default of the duty to appoint the first auditor` MEANS
    IF `s 205 helper: default in an act due by the last day`
          `the directors have appointed an accounting entity or accounting entities as the auditor or auditors of the company`
          `the day the directors made the appointment`
          (`s 205(1) the last day for the directors to appoint the first auditor` `the date the company was incorporated`)
          `the day as at which the question is asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors of a company must, within 3 months after incorporation of the company, appoint an accounting entity or accounting entities" -- a duty met in time, or not yet due: the provision's own question (fork line F-D1)

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the director must appoint within 3 months after incorporation. The trace clock counts days from incorporation.
-- src:19073 | 205.—(1) The directors of a company must, within 3 months after
-- src:19074 | incorporation of the company, appoint an accounting entity or
-- src:19075 | accounting entities to be the auditor or auditors of the company, and
-- src:19076 | any auditor or auditors so appointed hold office, subject to this
-- src:19077 | section, until the conclusion of the first annual general meeting.
@ref s 205(1) (src:19073-19077)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205 act`
`s 205(1) the directors must appoint the first auditor` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 205(1) appoint an accounting entity or accounting entities as the auditor or auditors of the company`
    WITHIN `s 205 helper: the days from the event to the last day` `the date the company was incorporated` (`s 205(1) the last day for the directors to appoint the first auditor` `the date the company was incorporated`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not appoint an accounting entity as auditor within 3 months after incorporation"

-- "any auditor or auditors so appointed hold office, subject to this section, until the conclusion of the first annual general meeting":
-- an "until" bar (the periods ruling's plain variants of "if"): before the conclusion, yes; after it, no. "Subject to this section":
-- an office already ended by removal (s 205(4)) or resignation (ss 205AA, 205AB) is ended.
-- src:19073 | 205.—(1) The directors of a company must, within 3 months after
-- src:19074 | incorporation of the company, appoint an accounting entity or
-- src:19075 | accounting entities to be the auditor or auditors of the company, and
-- src:19076 | any auditor or auditors so appointed hold office, subject to this
-- src:19077 | section, until the conclusion of the first annual general meeting.
@ref s 205(1) (src:19073-19077)
GIVEN `the first annual general meeting of the company has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor's office has already ended by removal or resignation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(1) the auditor appointed by the directors holds office` MEANS
    IF `the first annual general meeting of the company has concluded`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "hold office, subject to this section, until the conclusion of the first annual general meeting" (an "until" bar)
    ELSE (IF `the auditor's office has already ended by removal or resignation`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "hold office, subject to this section" (an office ended by removal under subsection (4) or resignation is not held: fork line F-T1)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 205(2): the company's duty to appoint at each annual general meeting`

-- src:19081 | (2) A company must at each annual general meeting of the
-- src:19082 | company appoint an accounting entity or accounting entities to be
-- src:19083 | the auditor or auditors of the company, and any auditor or auditors so
-- src:19084 | appointed hold office, subject to this section, until the conclusion of
-- src:19085 | the next annual general meeting of the company.
@ref s 205(2) (src:19081-19085)
GIVEN `an annual general meeting of the company has been held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company appointed an accounting entity or accounting entities as the auditor or auditors at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(2) the company is in default of the duty to appoint an auditor at the annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF `an annual general meeting of the company has been held` AND (NOT `the company appointed an accounting entity or accounting entities as the auditor or auditors at the meeting`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must at each annual general meeting of the company appoint an accounting entity or accounting entities" -- a duty met, or no meeting held yet: the provision's own question (fork line F-D1)

-- The duty as a regulative rule. The text fixes no time but the meeting itself and no consequence: no breach path (NOTES.md).
-- src:19081 | (2) A company must at each annual general meeting of the
-- src:19082 | company appoint an accounting entity or accounting entities to be
-- src:19083 | the auditor or auditors of the company, and any auditor or auditors so
-- src:19084 | appointed hold office, subject to this section, until the conclusion of
-- src:19085 | the next annual general meeting of the company.
@ref s 205(2) (src:19081-19085)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205 act`
`s 205(2) the company must appoint an auditor at each annual general meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 205(2) appoint an accounting entity or accounting entities as the auditor or auditors at the annual general meeting`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 205(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not appoint an accounting entity as auditor at the annual general meeting" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- src:19081 | (2) A company must at each annual general meeting of the
-- src:19082 | company appoint an accounting entity or accounting entities to be
-- src:19083 | the auditor or auditors of the company, and any auditor or auditors so
-- src:19084 | appointed hold office, subject to this section, until the conclusion of
-- src:19085 | the next annual general meeting of the company.
@ref s 205(2) (src:19081-19085)
GIVEN `the next annual general meeting of the company has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor's office has already ended by removal or resignation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(2) the auditor appointed at the annual general meeting holds office` MEANS
    IF `the next annual general meeting of the company has concluded`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "hold office, subject to this section, until the conclusion of the next annual general meeting of the company" (an "until" bar)
    ELSE (IF `the auditor's office has already ended by removal or resignation`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "hold office, subject to this section" (fork line F-T1)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 205(3): filling a casual vacancy`

-- src:19089 | (3) Subject to subsections (7) and (8) and section 205AF, the
-- src:19090 | directors may appoint an accounting entity to fill any casual vacancy
-- src:19091 | in the office of auditor of the company, but while such a vacancy
-- src:19092 | continues the surviving or continuing auditor or auditors (if any) may
-- src:19093 | act.
@ref s 205(3) (src:19089-19093)
GIVEN `there is a casual vacancy in the office of auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or firm to be appointed is an accounting entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (7) or (8) or section 205AF governs how this vacancy is to be filled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(3) the directors may appoint the accounting entity to fill the casual vacancy` MEANS
    IF `subsection (7) or (8) or section 205AF governs how this vacancy is to be filled`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to subsections (7) and (8) and section 205AF" -- those provisions, not this one, say who fills the vacancy they deal with (fork line F-G1)
    ELSE (IF `there is a casual vacancy in the office of auditor of the company` AND `the person or firm to be appointed is an accounting entity`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "to fill any casual vacancy" by "an accounting entity"; the subsection does not say the directors may not appoint otherwise (the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1)

-- src:19089 | (3) Subject to subsections (7) and (8) and section 205AF, the
-- src:19090 | directors may appoint an accounting entity to fill any casual vacancy
-- src:19091 | in the office of auditor of the company, but while such a vacancy
-- src:19092 | continues the surviving or continuing auditor or auditors (if any) may
-- src:19093 | act.
@ref s 205(3) (src:19089-19093)
GIVEN `a casual vacancy in the office of auditor of the company continues` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a surviving or continuing auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(3) the surviving or continuing auditor may act` MEANS
    IF `a casual vacancy in the office of auditor of the company continues` AND `there is a surviving or continuing auditor of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "while such a vacancy continues the surviving or continuing auditor or auditors (if any) may act" grants the power for the time of the vacancy; it does not say they may not act after it (a "may" with an "if"-variant gate: the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1)

§ `Section 205(4): removal of an auditor`

-- src:19097 | (4) An auditor of a company may be removed from office by
-- src:19098 | resolution of the company at a general meeting of which special
-- src:19099 | notice has been given, but not otherwise.
@ref s 205(4) (src:19097-19099)
GIVEN `the company has passed a resolution to remove the auditor at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `special notice of the resolution has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(4) the auditor may be removed from office by the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the company has passed a resolution to remove the auditor at a general meeting` AND `special notice of the resolution has been given`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be removed from office by resolution of the company at a general meeting of which special notice has been given, but not otherwise" (a grant the text closes with "but not otherwise")

§ `Section 205(5): notice of the removal resolution, and the auditor's representations`

-- src:19101 | (5) Where special notice of a resolution to remove an auditor is
-- src:19102 | received by a company —
-- src:19104 | (a) it must immediately send a copy of the notice to the auditor
-- src:19105 | concerned and to the Registrar; and
@ref s 205(5)(a) (src:19101-19105)
GIVEN `special notice of a resolution to remove an auditor has been received by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company sent a copy of the notice to the auditor concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company sent a copy of the notice to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company sent the copies immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(5)(a) the company is in default of the duty to send a copy of the notice` MEANS
    IF     `special notice of a resolution to remove an auditor has been received by the company`
       AND (NOT (    `the company sent a copy of the notice to the auditor concerned`
                 AND `the company sent a copy of the notice to the Registrar`
                 AND `the company sent the copies immediately`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where special notice of a resolution to remove an auditor is received by a company -- (a) it must immediately send a copy of the notice to the auditor concerned and to the Registrar" -- a duty met, or no notice received: the provision's own question (fork line F-D1)

-- "immediately" is a time the text states without a number: the time allowed is the s 52 input `the period of all convenient speed, as found` (notes/lest-without-deadline.md), so a late act reaches BREACH.
-- src:19101 | (5) Where special notice of a resolution to remove an auditor is
-- src:19102 | received by a company —
-- src:19104 | (a) it must immediately send a copy of the notice to the auditor
-- src:19105 | concerned and to the Registrar; and
@ref s 205(5)(a) (src:19101-19105)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205 act`
`s 205(5)(a) the company must send a copy of the notice of the removal resolution` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 205(5)(a) send a copy of the notice of the resolution to remove the auditor to the auditor concerned and to the Registrar`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- the section says "immediately"; read as Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send a copy of the notice of the removal resolution to the auditor and the Registrar"

-- (5)(b): the auditor "may, within 7 days after the receipt by the auditor of the copy of the notice, make representations in writing to the
-- company (not exceeding a reasonable length) and request that, prior to the meeting ..., a copy of the representations be sent by the company
-- to every member ...". The 7 days is a period the text fixes in its own words: outside it, JUST FALSE (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)).
-- The two named complements ("in writing", "not exceeding a reasonable length") and the request "prior to the meeting" limit the grant: NOTHING.
-- src:19107 | (b) the auditor may, within 7 days after the receipt by the
-- src:19108 | auditor of the copy of the notice, make representations in
-- src:19109 | writing to the company (not exceeding a reasonable length)
-- src:19110 | and request that, prior to the meeting at which the
-- src:19111 | resolution is to be considered, a copy of the
-- src:19112 | representations be sent by the company to every member
-- src:19113 | of the company to whom notice of the meeting is sent.
@ref s 205(5)(b) (src:19107-19113)
GIVEN `the day the auditor received the copy of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the day the auditor made the representations` IS A DATE
      `the representations are in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representations do not exceed a reasonable length` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the auditor asked for a copy to be sent to the members` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting at which the resolution is to be considered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(5)(b) the auditor may make representations and have a copy sent to every member` MEANS
    IF NOT (`period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the auditor received the copy of the notice` `the day the auditor made the representations` 7 Days)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 7 days after the receipt by the auditor of the copy of the notice" (a period fixed in the text's own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); fork line F-P1)
    ELSE (IF     `the representations are in writing`
             AND `the representations do not exceed a reasonable length`
             AND `the day the auditor asked for a copy to be sent to the members` LESS THAN `the day of the meeting at which the resolution is to be considered`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "make representations in writing to the company (not exceeding a reasonable length) and request that, prior to the meeting ..., a copy ... be sent" names what the grant covers; it does not say representations otherwise made are barred (the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1)

§ `Section 205(6): sending the representations, and having them read out`

-- "Unless the Registrar on the application of the company otherwise orders" governs the whole sentence on one reading (fork line F-R1):
-- the company's duty and the auditor's right both fall away.
-- src:19118 | (6) Unless the Registrar on the application of the company
-- src:19119 | otherwise orders, the company must send a copy of the
-- src:19120 | representations as so requested and the auditor may, without
-- src:19121 | affecting the auditor’s right to be heard orally, require that the
-- src:19122 | representations be read out at the meeting.
@ref s 205(6) (src:19118-19122)
GIVEN `the auditor requested that a copy of the representations be sent to every member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar, on the application of the company, has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company sent a copy of the representations to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(6) the company is in default of the duty to send a copy of the representations` MEANS
    IF     `the auditor requested that a copy of the representations be sent to every member`
       AND (NOT `the Registrar, on the application of the company, has ordered otherwise`)
       AND (NOT `the company sent a copy of the representations to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the Registrar on the application of the company otherwise orders, the company must send a copy of the representations as so requested" (an "unless" met, or the duty done, or no request: the provision's own question)

-- The text states no time and no consequence: the time allowed is the s 52 input `the period of all convenient speed, as found` (notes/lest-without-deadline.md), so a late act reaches BREACH.
-- src:19118 | (6) Unless the Registrar on the application of the company
-- src:19119 | otherwise orders, the company must send a copy of the
-- src:19120 | representations as so requested and the auditor may, without
-- src:19121 | affecting the auditor’s right to be heard orally, require that the
-- src:19122 | representations be read out at the meeting.
@ref s 205(6) (src:19118-19122)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205 act`
`s 205(6) the company must send a copy of the representations` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 205(6) send a copy of the representations to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send a copy of the representations to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent"

-- src:19118 | (6) Unless the Registrar on the application of the company
-- src:19119 | otherwise orders, the company must send a copy of the
-- src:19120 | representations as so requested and the auditor may, without
-- src:19121 | affecting the auditor’s right to be heard orally, require that the
-- src:19122 | representations be read out at the meeting.
@ref s 205(6) (src:19118-19122)
GIVEN `the auditor made representations as subsection (5)(b) allows` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar, on the application of the company, has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(6) the auditor may require that the representations be read out at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar, on the application of the company, has ordered otherwise`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the Registrar on the application of the company otherwise orders, ... the auditor may ... require that the representations be read out" (an "unless" met; on the reading that it governs both limbs: fork line F-R1)
    ELSE (IF `the auditor made representations as subsection (5)(b) allows`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is to have "the representations" read out; the subsection says nothing where the auditor made none (fork line F-G1)

§ `Section 205(7): where an auditor is removed, appointing another`

-- (a): at the meeting, by a resolution passed by a majority of not less than three-fourths of the members voting, in person or by proxy.
-- "Where" the auditor has been removed under (4) at a general meeting: a "where" gate on a "may" (split site (ii), ruling (b) of the
-- periods ruling: JUST FALSE; the grant rule leaves the "where" group for a lawyer: fork line F-W1). The three-fourths majority and
-- "another accounting entity nominated at the meeting" are named complements of the grant: NOTHING.
-- src:19124 | (7) Where an auditor of a company is removed from office pursuant
-- src:19125 | to subsection (4) at a general meeting of the company —
-- src:19127 | (a) the company may, at the meeting, by a resolution passed by
-- src:19128 | a majority of not less than three‑fourths of such members
-- src:19129 | of the company as being entitled to do so vote in person or,
-- src:19130 | where proxies are allowed, by proxy immediately appoint
-- src:19131 | another accounting entity nominated at the meeting as
-- src:19132 | auditor; or
@ref s 205(7)(a) (src:19124-19132)
GIVEN `an auditor of the company has been removed from office under subsection (4) at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or firm to be appointed is an accounting entity nominated at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members voting for the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members voting on the resolution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(7)(a) the company may immediately appoint another accounting entity as auditor` MEANS
    IF NOT `an auditor of the company has been removed from office under subsection (4) at a general meeting`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an auditor of a company is removed from office pursuant to subsection (4) at a general meeting of the company" (a "where" gate: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-W1)
    ELSE (IF     `the person or firm to be appointed is an accounting entity nominated at the meeting`
             AND `the number of members voting for the resolution` TIMES 4 AT LEAST `the number of members voting on the resolution` TIMES 3
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for "a resolution passed by a majority of not less than three-fourths" appointing "another accounting entity nominated at the meeting"; the paragraph does not bar another route, and paragraph (b) gives one (the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork lines F-G1, F-V1)

-- (b): the meeting adjourned to a date not earlier than 20 days and not later than 30 days after the meeting; an ordinary resolution appointing
-- an accounting entity whose nomination notice the company received at least 10 days before the resumption. The two periods are fixed in the
-- text's own words: outside them, JUST FALSE (item (a) of the periods ruling).
-- src:19134 | (b) the meeting may be adjourned to a date not earlier than
-- src:19135 | 20 days and not later than 30 days after the meeting and the
-- src:19136 | company may, by ordinary resolution, appoint another
-- src:19137 | accounting entity as auditor, being an accounting entity
-- src:19138 | notice of whose nomination as auditor has, at least 10 days
-- src:19139 | before the resumption of the adjourned meeting, been
-- src:19140 | received by the company.
@ref s 205(7)(b) (src:19134-19140)
GIVEN `an auditor of the company has been removed from office under subsection (4) at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the day the adjourned meeting resumes` IS A DATE
      `the day the company received notice of the nomination as auditor` IS A DATE
      `the person or firm to be appointed is an accounting entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is made by ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(7)(b) the company may appoint another accounting entity as auditor at the adjourned meeting` MEANS
    IF NOT `an auditor of the company has been removed from office under subsection (4) at a general meeting`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an auditor of a company is removed from office pursuant to subsection (4) at a general meeting" (a "where" gate: fork line F-W1)
    ELSE (IF NOT (    `the day the adjourned meeting resumes` AT LEAST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the meeting` 20 Days)
                  AND `the day the adjourned meeting resumes` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the meeting` 30 Days))
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "adjourned to a date not earlier than 20 days and not later than 30 days after the meeting" (a period fixed in the text's own words: item (a) of the periods ruling; fork line F-P1)
          ELSE (IF NOT (`period: the date is at least a period before` `the day the company received notice of the nomination as auditor` `the day the adjourned meeting resumes` 10 Days)
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "notice of whose nomination as auditor has, at least 10 days before the resumption of the adjourned meeting, been received by the company" (a period fixed in the text's own words: fork line F-P1)
                ELSE (IF `the person or firm to be appointed is an accounting entity` AND `the appointment is made by ordinary resolution`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE NOTHING)))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "by ordinary resolution" to "another accounting entity" (the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1)

§ `Section 205(8): notice of the removal to the Registrar, and the Registrar's appointment`

-- src:19144 | (8) A company must, immediately after the removal of an auditor
-- src:19145 | from office pursuant to subsection (4), give written notice of the
-- src:19146 | removal to the Registrar and, if the company does not appoint another
-- src:19147 | auditor under subsection (7), the Registrar may appoint an auditor.
@ref s 205(8) (src:19144-19147)
GIVEN `an auditor of the company has been removed from office under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company gave written notice of the removal to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company gave the notice immediately after the removal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(8) the company is in default of the duty to give written notice of the removal to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF     `an auditor of the company has been removed from office under subsection (4)`
       AND (NOT (`the company gave written notice of the removal to the Registrar` AND `the company gave the notice immediately after the removal`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must, immediately after the removal of an auditor from office pursuant to subsection (4), give written notice of the removal to the Registrar" (a duty met, or no removal: the provision's own question)

-- "immediately": no number, so the time allowed is the s 52 input `the period of all convenient speed, as found` (notes/lest-without-deadline.md), so a late act reaches BREACH.
-- src:19144 | (8) A company must, immediately after the removal of an auditor
-- src:19145 | from office pursuant to subsection (4), give written notice of the
-- src:19146 | removal to the Registrar and, if the company does not appoint another
-- src:19147 | auditor under subsection (7), the Registrar may appoint an auditor.
@ref s 205(8) (src:19144-19147)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205 act`
`s 205(8) the company must give written notice of the removal to the Registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 205(8) give written notice of the removal of the auditor to the Registrar`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- the section says "immediately after the removal"; read as Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not give the Registrar written notice of the removal of the auditor"

@ref s 205(8) (src:19144-19147)
GIVEN `an auditor of the company has been removed from office under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has appointed another auditor under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(8) the Registrar may appoint an auditor of the company` MEANS
    IF `an auditor of the company has been removed from office under subsection (4)` AND (NOT `the company has appointed another auditor under subsection (7)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company does not appoint another auditor under subsection (7), the Registrar may appoint an auditor" grants the power for that case and says nothing of any other (the grant rule of 2026-11-12: a "may" whose "if" gate failed; fork line F-G1)

§ `Section 205(9): the term of an auditor appointed under (7) or (8)`

-- src:19151 | (9) An auditor appointed pursuant to subsection (7) or (8) must,
-- src:19152 | subject to this section, hold office until the conclusion of the next
-- src:19153 | annual general meeting of the company.
@ref s 205(9) (src:19151-19153)
GIVEN `the next annual general meeting of the company has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor's office has already ended by removal or resignation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(9) the auditor appointed under subsection (7) or (8) holds office` MEANS
    IF `the next annual general meeting of the company has concluded`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, subject to this section, hold office until the conclusion of the next annual general meeting of the company" (an "until" bar)
    ELSE (IF `the auditor's office has already ended by removal or resignation`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to this section" (fork line F-T1)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 205(10): the Registrar's appointment on a member's application`

-- src:19155 | (10) If the directors do not appoint an auditor or auditors as required
-- src:19156 | by this section, the Registrar may on the application in writing of any
-- src:19157 | member of the company make the appointment.
@ref s 205(10) (src:19155-19157)
GIVEN `the directors have not appointed an auditor or auditors as section 205 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member of the company has applied in writing for the Registrar to make the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(10) the Registrar may make the appointment on the application of a member` MEANS
    IF `the directors have not appointed an auditor or auditors as section 205 requires` AND `a member of the company has applied in writing for the Registrar to make the appointment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the directors do not appoint an auditor or auditors as required by this section, the Registrar may on the application in writing of any member of the company make the appointment" (a "may" whose "if" gate failed: the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1)

§ `Section 205(11): who can be appointed at an annual general meeting`

-- src:19159 | (11) Subject to subsection (7), an accounting entity is not capable of
-- src:19160 | being appointed auditor of a company at an annual general meeting
-- src:19161 | unless it held office as auditor of the company immediately before the
-- src:19162 | meeting or notice of its nomination as auditor was given to the
-- src:19167 | company by a member of the company not less than 21 days before
-- src:19168 | the meeting.
@ref s 205(11) (src:19159-19168)
GIVEN `the appointment is made under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounting entity held office as auditor of the company immediately before the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member of the company gave the company notice of the accounting entity's nomination as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the member gave notice of the nomination` IS A DATE
      `the day of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(11) the accounting entity is capable of being appointed auditor at the annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the appointment is made under subsection (7)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (7)" -- an appointment under subsection (7) is governed by it, and this subsection says nothing of it (fork line F-G1)
    ELSE (IF     `the accounting entity held office as auditor of the company immediately before the meeting`
              OR (    `a member of the company gave the company notice of the accounting entity's nomination as auditor`
                  AND `period: the date is at least a period before` `the day the member gave notice of the nomination` `the day of the annual general meeting` 21 Days)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an accounting entity is not capable of being appointed auditor of a company at an annual general meeting unless it held office as auditor of the company immediately before the meeting or notice of its nomination as auditor was given to the company by a member of the company not less than 21 days before the meeting" (an "unless")

§ `Section 205(12): sending a copy of the notice of nomination`

-- src:19172 | (12) Where notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an
-- src:19173 | auditor of a company is received by the company whether for
-- src:19174 | appointment at an adjourned meeting under subsection (7) or at an
-- src:19175 | annual general meeting, the company must, not less than 7 days
-- src:19176 | before the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting, send a
-- src:19177 | copy of the notice to the accounting entity nominated, to each auditor
-- src:19178 | (if any) of the company and to each person entitled to receive notice
-- src:19179 | of general meetings of the company.
@ref s 205(12) (src:19172-19179)
GIVEN `the day of the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 205(12) the last day for the company to send a copy of the notice of nomination` MEANS
    `period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the day of the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting` 7 Days

-- src:19172 | (12) Where notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an
-- src:19173 | auditor of a company is received by the company whether for
-- src:19174 | appointment at an adjourned meeting under subsection (7) or at an
-- src:19175 | annual general meeting, the company must, not less than 7 days
-- src:19176 | before the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting, send a
-- src:19177 | copy of the notice to the accounting entity nominated, to each auditor
-- src:19178 | (if any) of the company and to each person entitled to receive notice
-- src:19179 | of general meetings of the company.
@ref s 205(12) (src:19172-19179)
GIVEN `notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an auditor has been received by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the company has sent a copy of the notice to the accounting entity nominated, to each auditor (if any) and to each person entitled to receive notice of general meetings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company sent the copies` IS A DATE
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(12) the company is in default of the duty to send a copy of the notice of nomination` MEANS
    IF     `notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an auditor has been received by the company`
       AND `s 205 helper: default in an act due by the last day`
              `the company has sent a copy of the notice to the accounting entity nominated, to each auditor (if any) and to each person entitled to receive notice of general meetings`
              `the day the company sent the copies`
              (`s 205(12) the last day for the company to send a copy of the notice of nomination` `the day of the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting`)
              `the day as at which the question is asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must, not less than 7 days before the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting, send a copy of the notice" (a duty met in time, or not yet due, or no notice received: the provision's own question; subsection (13) may deem it met: fork line F-D1)

-- The duty as a regulative rule. The trace clock counts days from the day the company received the notice of nomination.
-- src:19172 | (12) Where notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an
-- src:19173 | auditor of a company is received by the company whether for
-- src:19174 | appointment at an adjourned meeting under subsection (7) or at an
-- src:19175 | annual general meeting, the company must, not less than 7 days
-- src:19176 | before the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting, send a
-- src:19177 | copy of the notice to the accounting entity nominated, to each auditor
-- src:19178 | (if any) of the company and to each person entitled to receive notice
-- src:19179 | of general meetings of the company.
@ref s 205(12) (src:19172-19179)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the day the company received the notice of nomination` IS A DATE
      `the day of the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205 act`
`s 205(12) the company must send a copy of the notice of nomination` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 205(12) send a copy of the notice of nomination to the accounting entity nominated, to each auditor and to each person entitled to receive notice of general meetings`
    WITHIN `s 205 helper: the days from the event to the last day` `the day the company received the notice of nomination` (`s 205(12) the last day for the company to send a copy of the notice of nomination` `the day of the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send a copy of the notice of nomination not less than 7 days before the meeting"

§ `Section 205(12A): a company that need not hold an annual general meeting`

-- Where the company need not hold an AGM (s 175A(1)) and the auditors are to be appointed by a resolution by written means (s 184A, by virtue of
-- s 175A(10)), the references in (11) and (12) to the date of an AGM are references to the time (a) agreement to the resolution is sought under
-- s 184C, or (b) the documents in s 183(3A) are served or made accessible, "as the case may be". The functions here are the answer the other
-- subsections' day input takes. Where the conditions fail the answer is NOTHING: the subsection says nothing of the date of a meeting that is held.
-- src:19183 | (12A) Where a company need not hold an annual general meeting
-- src:19184 | for a financial year because of section 175A(1) and the auditor or
-- src:19185 | auditors of the company is or are to be appointed by a resolution by
-- src:19186 | written means under section 184A by virtue of section 175A(10),
-- src:19187 | references in subsections (11) and (12) to the date of an annual
-- src:19188 | general meeting are references to the time —
-- src:19190 | (a) agreement to that resolution is sought in accordance with
-- src:19191 | section 184C; or
-- src:19193 | (b) documents referred to in section 183(3A) in respect of the
-- src:19194 | resolution are served or made accessible in accordance
-- src:19195 | with section 183(3A),
-- src:19197 | as the case may be.
@ref s 205(12A) (src:19183-19197)
GIVEN `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year because of section 175A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditors are to be appointed by a resolution by written means under section 184A by virtue of section 175A(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `agreement to the resolution is sought in accordance with section 184C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day agreement to the resolution is sought` IS A DATE
      `the day the documents referred to in section 183(3A) are served or made accessible` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 205(12A) the day that stands for the date of the annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year because of section 175A(1)` AND `the auditors are to be appointed by a resolution by written means under section 184A by virtue of section 175A(10)`
    THEN (IF `agreement to the resolution is sought in accordance with section 184C`
          THEN JUST `the day agreement to the resolution is sought`
          ELSE JUST `the day the documents referred to in section 183(3A) are served or made accessible`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company need not hold an annual general meeting ... and the auditor or auditors ... are to be appointed by a resolution by written means" -- the subsection does not say what the date is where its "where" does not hold

§ `Section 205(13): short notice of an annual general meeting`

-- src:19201 | (13) If, after notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an
-- src:19202 | auditor of a company has been given to the company, the annual
-- src:19203 | general meeting of the company is called for a date 21 days or less
-- src:19204 | after the notice has been given, subsection (11) does not apply in
-- src:19205 | relation to the accounting entity and, if the annual general meeting is
-- src:19206 | called for a date not more than 7 days after the notice has been given
-- src:19207 | and a copy of the notice is, at the time notice of the meeting is given,
-- src:19208 | sent to each person to whom, under subsection (12), it is required to
-- src:19209 | be sent, the company is deemed to have complied with that subsection
-- src:19210 | in relation to the notice.
@ref s 205(13) (src:19201-19210)
GIVEN `notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an auditor has been given to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice of nomination was given` IS A DATE
      `the date for which the annual general meeting is called` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(13) subsection (11) does not apply in relation to the accounting entity` MEANS
    IF     `notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an auditor has been given to the company`
       AND `the date for which the annual general meeting is called` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the notice of nomination was given` 21 Days)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, after notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an auditor of a company has been given to the company, the annual general meeting of the company is called for a date 21 days or less after the notice has been given, subsection (11) does not apply" (an "if" gate; a failed "if" counts as the text's no: marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1)

@ref s 205(13) (src:19201-19210)
GIVEN `notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an auditor has been given to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice of nomination was given` IS A DATE
      `the date for which the annual general meeting is called` IS A DATE
      `a copy of the notice was sent, at the time notice of the meeting was given, to each person to whom subsection (12) requires it to be sent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(13) the company is deemed to have complied with subsection (12)` MEANS
    IF     `notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an auditor has been given to the company`
       AND `the date for which the annual general meeting is called` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the notice of nomination was given` 7 Days)
       AND `a copy of the notice was sent, at the time notice of the meeting was given, to each person to whom subsection (12) requires it to be sent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the annual general meeting is called for a date not more than 7 days after the notice has been given and a copy of the notice is, at the time notice of the meeting is given, sent to each person ..., the company is deemed to have complied with that subsection" (an "if" gate; marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1)

§ `Section 205(16): who fixes the auditor's fees and expenses`

DECLARE `s 205(16) who appointed the auditor` IS ONE OF
    `s 205(16)(a) the company at a general meeting`
    `s 205(16)(b) the directors`
    `s 205(16)(b) the Registrar`

DECLARE `s 205(16) who fixed the fees and expenses` IS ONE OF
    `s 205(16) fixed by the company in general meeting`
    `s 205(16) fixed by the directors`
    `s 205(16) fixed by the Registrar`
    `s 205(16) not fixed`

-- (a): an auditor appointed by the company at a general meeting: fees and expenses "must be fixed by the company in general meeting or, if so
-- authorised by the members at the last preceding annual general meeting, by the directors". (b): an auditor appointed by the directors or
-- the Registrar (under s 205 or s 205AF): "may be fixed by the directors or by the Registrar, as the case may be and, if not so fixed, must be
-- fixed as provided in paragraph (a) as if the auditor had been appointed by the company".
-- src:19221 | (16) The fees and expenses of an auditor of a company —
-- src:19223 | (a) in the case of an auditor appointed by the company at a
-- src:19224 | general meeting — must be fixed by the company in
-- src:19225 | general meeting or, if so authorised by the members at the
-- src:19226 | last preceding annual general meeting, by the directors;
-- src:19227 | and
-- src:19229 | (b) in the case of an auditor appointed by the directors or by
-- src:19230 | the Registrar under this section or under
-- src:19231 | section 205AF — may be fixed by the directors or by
-- src:19232 | the Registrar, as the case may be, and, if not so fixed, must
-- src:19233 | be fixed as provided in paragraph (a) as if the auditor had
-- src:19234 | been appointed by the company.
@ref s 205(16) (src:19221-19234)
GIVEN `appointed by` IS A `s 205(16) who appointed the auditor`
      `fixed by` IS A `s 205(16) who fixed the fees and expenses`
      `the members authorised the directors to fix them at the last preceding annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(16) the fees and expenses of the auditor are fixed as the subsection requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `appointed by`
    WHEN `s 205(16)(a) the company at a general meeting` THEN
        (CONSIDER `fixed by`
         WHEN `s 205(16) fixed by the company in general meeting` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 205(16) fixed by the directors` THEN (IF `the members authorised the directors to fix them at the last preceding annual general meeting` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
         WHEN `s 205(16) fixed by the Registrar` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `s 205(16) not fixed` THEN JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be fixed by the company in general meeting or, if so authorised by the members at the last preceding annual general meeting, by the directors" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)
    WHEN `s 205(16)(b) the directors` THEN
        (CONSIDER `fixed by`
         WHEN `s 205(16) fixed by the directors` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 205(16) fixed by the Registrar` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `s 205(16) fixed by the company in general meeting` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 205(16) not fixed` THEN JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be fixed by the directors or by the Registrar, as the case may be and, if not so fixed, must be fixed as provided in paragraph (a)" (fixed by the Registrar for an auditor the directors appointed is not "as the case may be"; not fixed at all is not (a) either)
    WHEN `s 205(16)(b) the Registrar` THEN
        (CONSIDER `fixed by`
         WHEN `s 205(16) fixed by the Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 205(16) fixed by the directors` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `s 205(16) fixed by the company in general meeting` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 205(16) not fixed` THEN JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be fixed by the directors or by the Registrar, as the case may be and, if not so fixed, must be fixed as provided in paragraph (a)"

§ `Section 205(17): the offence`

-- src:19238 | (17) If default is made in complying with this section, the company
-- src:19239 | and every director of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:19240 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:19241 | $5,000.
@ref s 205(17) (src:19238-19241)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 205` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 205(17) person charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(17) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 205`
    THEN (CONSIDER person
          WHEN `s 205(17) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 205(17) a director of the company who is in default` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 205(17) any other person` THEN JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company and every director of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" names the persons it makes guilty; a person outside the class is not made guilty by it (the offence's own question; split site (i), fork line F-E1)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section" (an unmet element of the offence: split site (i), fork line F-E1)

@ref s 205(17) (src:19238-19241)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 205` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 205(17) person charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 205(17) the most the person may be fined on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 205(17) the person is guilty of the offence` `default is made in complying with section 205` person EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST 5000
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty
